 ownership models (Go SIG owning vs. comms/docs owning), required access (“keys”), and operational processes (DNS change notifications, rollout, playbooks).\\n\\n  - Tyler: Outline notification/subscription approach for DNS/CAA changes affecting serving; suggest checks-and-balances process.\\n\\n  - Group: Align on clear owner, permissions, and ops plan before any platform migration decision.\\n\\n### 2) PR: Add internal observability to OTLP Trace gRPC package; instrumentation scope naming\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - PR introduces internal observability instrumentation to the OTLP Trace gRPC package.\\n\\n  - Debate on scope name: use the instrumentation library/package path (current proposal) vs. the instrumented package/component name.\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Specification guidance: instrumentation scope name should reflect the instrumentation library (not the instrumented target). Current proposal aligns with spec.\\n\\n  - Concern about stability: using internal package paths can constrain future internal code reorganization if dashboards/processors depend on the scope name.\\n\\n  - Proposal to add an attribute indicating the “instrumented component/package” to aid filtering/search, while keeping the scope name aligned with spec.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - Proceed with scope name per spec (instrumentation library).\\n\\n  - Consider adding an attribute to identify the instrumented component in a follow-up, potentially informed by spec work.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - Tyler: Resolve the review thread referencing spec guidance; request/collect approvals.\\n\\n  - Robert: Open/track a semantic conventions issue to define an attribute for “instrumented component” across instrumentation.\\n\\n  - Group: Review PR; provide approvals.\\n\\n### 3) PR: Error type improvements (semantic conventions alignment)\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - Improve error typing so the error.type attribute reflects domain-specific values (e.g., gRPC status, partial error details) rather than generic “error string.”\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Parser update allows passing errors that return a domain-relevant “type” string for telemetry.\\n\\n  - Fallback remains to package/type name if no domain-specific type is available.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - General agreement on direction; proceed after minor doc checks.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - Robert: Verify GoDoc/rendering for the error type interface/docs (e.g., lines noted in error_type.go); approve once confirmed.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"damien creat a communiti issu to drive a cross team ownership and oper propos invit gc govern committe comm doc team collector maintain go instrument ebpf instrument ebpf profil and this sig damien propos strawman ownership model go sig own v comm doc own requir access key and oper process dns chang notif rollout playbook tyler outlin notif subscript approach for dns caa chang affect serv suggest check and balanc process group align on clear owner permiss and op plan befor ani platform migrat decis 2 pr add intern observ to otlp trace grpc packag instrument scope name summari pr introduc intern observ instrument to the otlp trace grpc packag debat on scope name use the instrument librari packag path current propos v the instrument packag compon name discuss highlight specif guidanc instrument scope name should reflect the instrument librari not the instrument target current propos align with spec concern about stabil use intern packag path can constrain futur intern code reorgan if dashboard processor depend on the scope name propos to add an attribut indic the instrument compon packag to aid filter search while keep the scope name align with spec decis proceed with scope name per spec instrument librari consid ad an attribut to identifi the instrument compon in a follow up potenti inform by spec work action item tyler resolv the review thread referenc spec guidanc request collect approv robert open track a semant convent issu to defin an attr